-- title:
--   Lemma D.1 — along CBA, $\pi_{\mathcal C}(u_t)\ne0$ persists; along CBA$^+$, $u_t\ne0$ persists
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal X\subset\mathbb R^n$ be a nonempty convex compact set, $\kappa=\max_{x\in\mathcal X}\|x\|_2$, $\mathcal C=\operatorname{cone}(\{\kappa\}\times\mathcal X)$ and $\pi_{\mathcal C}$ the projection onto $\mathcal C$. Let $x_0,x_1\in\mathcal X$, let $(\omega_t)_{t\ge1}$ be payoff weights and $(f_t)_{t\ge1}$ losses.
--
--   1. Let $(u_t)$ be the aggregate payoffs of CBA with weights $\omega$ on the payoffs, and $t\ge1$. If $\pi_{\mathcal C}(u_t)\neq0$, then $\pi_{\mathcal C}(u_{t'})\neq0$ for all $t'\ge t$.
--   2. Let $(u_t)$ be the aggregate payoffs of CBA$^+$ with weights $\omega$ on the payoffs, and $t\ge1$. If $u_t\neq0$, then $u_{t'}\neq0$ for all $t'\ge t$.
--
--   Once the algorithm has taken a non-degenerate decision, all later ones are non-degenerate as well. This is the first case of the proof of Theorem 3.6: a zero aggregate payoff at round $t$ forces a zero one at round $t-1$, so both decisions equal the default point $x_0$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The CBA run is `cbaU`, the CBA$^+$ run the published `ConicBlackwell.cbaPlusU` (starting from $u_0=0$, $u_1=\pi_{\mathcal C}(\omega_1v_1)$, as in the published mission); $\pi_{\mathcal C}$ is `PerspEpi.projC`. The weights are arbitrary reals.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: weights (ω_t)_{t≥1}, positive in the paper → arbitrary real ω; reason: the argument (p.25) uses ⟨π_C(u_t), v_{t+1}⟩ = 0 and ⟨u_t, v_{t+1}⟩ = 0, which hold for every ω; the positive weights are a special case
--   - encoding: the CBA+ run of Algorithm 1 → the published ConicBlackwell.cbaPlusU, which starts from u₀ = 0 with u₁ = π_C(ω₁v₁); reason: the published mission's correction of line 4 (the printed u₁ = ω₁v₁ can leave C); the two agree whenever ω₁v₁ ∈ C
--   - encoding: x₁ ∈ X (initialization) and x₀ ∈ X 'arbitrary' in CHOOSEDECISION → universally quantified parameters in X; reason: the claim holds for every choice
--   - encoding: π_C, κ = max ‖x‖₂, ℝⁿ⁺¹ → PerspEpi.projC (cone (lift (kappa X) '' X)), kappa X (sSup), E (n + 1); reason: C is nonempty closed convex, so projC is the projection; sSup is the max on a nonempty compact X
-- source:
--   Grand-Clément & Kroer, Solving Optimization Problems with Blackwell Approachability, arXiv:2202.12277v1 (https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.12277v1), Lemma D.1, p.25 (proof p.25)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ApproachRegret_ToOLO_AlgorithmOne
import Definitions.Def_PerspEpi_projC
import Definitions.Def_ConicBlackwell_cbaPlusU
import Definitions.Def_ConicBlackwell_Supplement_cbaU
open scoped RealInnerProductSpace
open ApproachRegret.ToOLO

namespace ConicBlackwell.Supplement

/-- **Lemma D.1**, Grand-Clément & Kroer, arXiv:2202.12277v1, p.25.
1. Let `(u_t)` be the payoffs generated by CBA with weights `(ω_t)` on the payoffs, and `t ≥ 1`.
   If `π_C(u_t) ≠ 0`, then `π_C(u_{t'}) ≠ 0` for all `t' ≥ t`.
2. Let `(u_t)` be the payoffs generated by CBA+ with weights `(ω_t)` on the payoffs, and `t ≥ 1`.
   If `u_t ≠ 0`, then `u_{t'} ≠ 0` for all `t' ≥ t`.

Formalization Note: `C = cone({κ} × X) = cone (lift (kappa X) '' X)`, `π_C = PerspEpi.projC C`
(the unique nearest point; it exists on the nonempty closed convex `C`).  The CBA run is `cbaU`,
the CBA+ run the published `ConicBlackwell.cbaPlusU`, both from `u₀ = 0`, an arbitrary first
decision `x₁ ∈ X` and the arbitrary point `x₀ ∈ X` of CHOOSEDECISION.  The weights `ω` are
arbitrary reals: the argument uses no sign of `ω`. -/
theorem lemma_D_1 {n : ℕ} (X : Set (E n)) (hXne : X.Nonempty) (hXc : IsCompact X)
    (hXcv : Convex ℝ X) (x₀ x₁ : E n) (hx₀ : x₀ ∈ X) (hx₁ : x₁ ∈ X)
    (ω : ℕ → ℝ) (f : ℕ → E n) :
    (∀ t, 1 ≤ t →
        PerspEpi.projC (cone (lift (kappa X) '' X)) (cbaU X x₀ x₁ ω f t) ≠ 0 →
          ∀ t', t ≤ t' →
            PerspEpi.projC (cone (lift (kappa X) '' X)) (cbaU X x₀ x₁ ω f t') ≠ 0) ∧
      (∀ t, 1 ≤ t → ConicBlackwell.cbaPlusU X x₀ x₁ ω f t ≠ 0 →
          ∀ t', t ≤ t' → ConicBlackwell.cbaPlusU X x₀ x₁ ω f t' ≠ 0) := by sorry

end ConicBlackwell.Supplement
